      "observed": "R3 and R4 are 0Ω resistors, while R13 and R14 are 1kΩ resistors.",
      "expected": "R3 and R4 should be 1kΩ series resistors for the PWM signal path, and R13/R14 should be 0Ω jumpers for the serial servo bus, per the design specification and the schematic note 'Short R13, R14 for Serial Servo'.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "R3, R4 | 1k each | Series resistors from the PWM1/PWM2 GPIO nets to J3 pin 3 / J8 pin 3 respectively."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "R13, R14 | 0 Ω (jumpers) | When shorted, bridge J3-pin3 and J8-pin3 together and onto the MAX3485 TTL bus"
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "Short R13, R14 for Serial Servo (sheet 1)"
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "R3 0; R13 1k (sheet 1)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "PWM mode loses the intended 1kΩ series protection on the GPIO-driven signal lines, while serial mode inserts 1kΩ in the shared half-duplex bus, attenuating and potentially disrupting serial servo communication.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C5", "C7"],
      "pins": ["C5.1", "C5.2", "C7.1", "C7.2"],
      "nets": ["servo power rail", "GND"],
      "observed": "C5 and C7 on the servo power rail are 100 nF (0.1 µF) capacitors.",
      "expected": "The servo power rail should have four 100 µF bulk capacitors (C1–C4) as specified.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C1–C4 | 100 µF × 4 | Bulk capacitance on the servo power rail (downstream of D2)"
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "C5 100n; C7 100n (sheet 1)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The servo power rail has only 200 µF of bulk capacitance instead of 400 µF, reducing its ability to buffer the high inrush current of PWM servos and increasing the risk of M5Stack brownouts as warned in the README.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic contains two clear value deviations from the specification: R3/R4 and R13/R14 have swapped/wrong values (0Ω vs 1kΩ), and two servo-rail bulk capacitors (C5, C7) are 100 nF instead of 100 µF, which would degrade PWM protection, serial signal integrity, and servo inrush buffering."
}

